+
+## Statement
+
+Assume the axiom of countable choice. Fix the compact non-Abelian group, its global form, local bundle sector, invariant quadratic form, matter representations, classical action, units, and boundary data selected by the adopted Yang–Mills model on oriented, time-oriented Minkowski space with signature $(-,+,+,+)$ and $x^0=ct$. Work in a local trivialization in natural units $c=\hbar=1$. The selected finite-jet field algebra has even gauge potential $A_\mu$ of engineering dimension one, ghost $c$ odd of ghost number one and dimension zero, matter fields in the model-supplied representations, and the optional nonminimal antighost $\bar c$ and auxiliary field $b$ with $(\operatorname{gh},\dim)(\bar c)=(-1,2)$ and $(\operatorname{gh},\dim)(b)=(0,2)$. Use the BRST convention $sA_\mu=\partial_\mu c+[A_\mu,c]$, $sc=-\tfrac12[c,c]$, $s\psi=-\rho(c)\psi$, $s\bar c=b$, and $sb=0$. Choose the linear Lorenz gauge $\partial^\mu A_\mu=0$ with parameter $\xi>0$, dimensional regularization $D=4-2\epsilon$, modified minimal subtraction, a finite engineering-dimension bound $d_*$ for local counterterms, and a formal dimensionless loop variable $\lambda$. The formal effective action is $\Gamma(\lambda)=\Gamma_0+\sum_{n\geq1}\lambda^n\Gamma_n$, where $\Gamma_0$ is an even ghost-number-zero classical BV functional satisfying the classical master equation $\tfrac12(\Gamma_0,\Gamma_0)=0$. Write $B_{\Gamma_0}X=(\Gamma_0,X)$ and $\mathfrak S(\Gamma)=\tfrac12(\Gamma,\Gamma)$.
+
+Assume the chosen renormalization data have the local Quantum Action Principle property: whenever the coefficientwise identity first fails at order $n$, its defect is $\mathfrak S(\Gamma^{(<n)})=\lambda^n\Delta_n+O(\lambda^{n+1})$ for a finite-jet local ghost-number-one functional $\Delta_n$. Assume also that the anomaly-cancellation data supply, as a sequence for all such orders, local ghost-number-zero functionals $\Xi_n$ and local ghost-number-one three-forms $\Theta_n$ satisfying $\Delta_n=B_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n+d_H\Theta_n$. Require compact support or boundary conditions that make integrated $d_H$-exact top forms vanish. Then a formal local counterterm series can be chosen so that the renormalized effective action satisfies $\mathfrak S(\Gamma(\lambda))=0$ coefficientwise. The local counterterm freedom, modulo BRST-exact terms and total derivatives, is exactly the restricted ghost-number-zero, form-degree-four cohomology of the specified finite-jet counterterm space; a nonzero ghost-number-one obstruction class cannot be removed by an allowed local counterterm. This is a conditional model deduction: it neither proves the QAP or anomaly-cancellation hypothesis nor computes a basis of either cohomology group. A finite-dimensional Faddeev–Popov Jacobian is only the ordinary Jacobian of a specified finite-dimensional regulated action and slice; this theorem does not identify it with a continuum functional determinant or assert a continuum measure, convergence, or nonperturbative Yang–Mills existence.
+
+## Statement references
+
+[Barnich, Brandt, and Henneaux, §§2.3 and 12.2–12.3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0002245)
+
+[Maas, §4.7.2 and §§5.2.7–5.2.8](https://static.uni-graz.at/fileadmin/_Persoenliche_Webseite/maas_axel/qftii2024.pdf)
+
+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** The selected Yang–Mills model, its local field and BV algebras, the formal regulator and counterterm space, and the hypotheses in the statement.
+
+[A1] The model postulate selects the compact global gauge group, bundle sector, metric, invariant quadratic form, matter content, units, action, boundary data, and physical scope. The current planned interface says these choices are adopted model inputs and do not imply a quantum continuum theory; its local item carrier is absent. [[post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model]]
+
+[F1] The formal perturbative data fix Lorenz gauge, $D=4-2\epsilon$ dimensional regularization, modified minimal subtraction, the ghost-number-zero finite-jet counterterm space, and the QAP locality condition. The QAP is an explicit property of the data, not a result imported from a scalar renormalization theorem. [[def-qftx-formal-perturbative-yang-mills-data]]
+
+[F2] The minimal BRST conventions are $sA_\mu=\partial_\mu c+[A_\mu,c]$, $sc=-\tfrac12[c,c]$, and $s\psi=-\rho(c)\psi$ on the stated finite-jet algebra. [[def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex]]
+
+[F3] Under the Lie-algebra Jacobi identity and representation identity, this finite-jet derivation satisfies $s^2=0$ and commutes with total derivatives. The current lemma's full proof was inspected; its current readiness record is missing. [[lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence]]
+
+[F4] The local BRST cohomology in bidegree $(g,p)$ is the quotient of local forms satisfying $sa+d_Hb=0$ by forms of the shape $sm+d_Hn$, with the declared compact-support or boundary interpretation at top degree. The definition carrier is current, but its Step-1 readiness record is missing. [[def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology]]
+
+[F5] The chosen odd antibracket has ghost number $+1$, shifted graded skew-symmetry, and the shifted Jacobi identity; the BV differential is $sF=(\Gamma_0,F)$. Its optional nonminimal pair has $s\bar c=b$ and $sb=0$, with no cohomological-contractibility claim. [[def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action]]
+
+[F6] For an even ghost-number-zero BV functional, the shifted Jacobi identity gives $s^2=0$ exactly when its classical master equation holds, under the stated no-ghost-number-one-center condition. [[lem-qftx-bv-master-equation-brst-nilpotence]]
+
+[F7] A finite-dimensional regulated gauge-slice datum defines $\Delta_{\mathrm{FP}}=|\det(d\chi\circ R_s)|$ only on the specified finite-dimensional slice; it makes no functional-measure assertion. This definition is used only for the finite-Jacobian boundary stated in the theorem. [[def-qftx-gauge-slice-and-faddeev-popov-operator]]
+
+[F8] The planned classical Yang–Mills supplier is to prove gauge invariance of the adopted action from that model and the local curvature/gauge formula, with boundary conditions. That theorem carrier is absent and is not claimed proved here. [[pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-classical-gauge-invariance]]
+
+[A2] The supplied classical BV functional $\Gamma_0$ satisfies $\tfrac12(\Gamma_0,\Gamma_0)=0$; the BV definition and master-equation lemma justify the nilpotent linearized operator used below. This condition is part of the formal datum and is not inferred from an uninspected master-action proof.
+
+[A3] At every perturbative order, the local defect is cohomologically trivial: a supplied sequence $(\Xi_n,\Theta_n)_{n\geq1}$ satisfies $\Delta_n=B_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n+d_H\Theta_n$. Supplying the sequence avoids any unrecorded countable choice in forming a formal counterterm series.
+
+[A4] Every integrated $d_H$-exact four-form in the proof vanishes by the stated compact-support or boundary condition.
+
+## Proof
+
+1.1 By [A2] and [F6], the linearized Slavnov operator $B_{\Gamma_0}$ is nilpotent on the stated BV algebra. [given, A2, F6, algebra]
+
+1.2 Fix an order $n$ after the lower-order coefficients have been chosen to satisfy the identity. By [F1], the first defect is a local functional $\Delta_n$ and $\mathfrak S(\Gamma^{(<n)})=\lambda^n\Delta_n+O(\lambda^{n+1})$. [given, F1]
+
+1.3 The antibracket Jacobi identity gives $(\Gamma^{(<n)},\mathfrak S(\Gamma^{(<n)}))=0$. Taking the coefficient of $\lambda^n$ and using $\Gamma^{(<n)}=\Gamma_0+O(\lambda)$ yields $(\Gamma_0,\Delta_n)=B_{\Gamma_0}\Delta_n=0$, the local consistency condition. [F5, step 1.2, algebra]
+
+2.1 By [A3], write $\Delta_n=B_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n+d_H\Theta_n$ and set $\Gamma^{(<n+1)}:=\Gamma^{(<n)}-\lambda^n\Xi_n$. Bilinearity of the antibracket gives $\mathfrak S(\Gamma^{(<n+1)})=\mathfrak S(\Gamma^{(<n)})-\lambda^nB_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n+O(\lambda^{n+1})=\lambda^n d_H\Theta_n+O(\lambda^{n+1})$. [A3, F5, step 1.2, algebra]
+
+2.2 Integrating the remaining defect removes $d_H\Theta_n$ by [A4], so the identity holds through order $n$. The supplied counterterm sequence makes $C(\lambda):=-\sum_{n\geq1}\lambda^n\Xi_n$ a well-defined formal local series; induction therefore yields a renormalized $\Gamma(\lambda)+C(\lambda)$ satisfying the Slavnov–Taylor identity coefficientwise, without any convergence claim. [A3, A4, step 2.1, algebra]
+
+3.1 Let $a_n$ be a local four-form in the allowed ghost-number-zero counterterm space. Its order-$n$ change preserves the Slavnov identity precisely when its linearized variation is a total derivative, $B_{\Gamma_0}a_n+d_Hb_{n-1}=0$ for some local three-form $b_{n-1}$. With $s:=B_{\Gamma_0}$ this is exactly the cocycle condition in [F4]. [A2, F4, F5, algebra]
+
+3.2 Two such counterterms represent the same freedom precisely when their difference is $sm+d_Hr$ for a local ghost-number-minus-one four-form $m$ and local ghost-number-zero three-form $r$, which is the denominator in [F4]. Thus the allowed local counterterm classes are exactly the restricted $H^{0,4}(s\mid d_H)$ classes; the same argument at ghost number one identifies the obstruction quotient, and a nonzero class cannot equal an allowed exact restoring term. [A3, F4, step 3.1, algebra] ∎
+
