+## Statement
+Use the formal perturbative renormalization datum specified for the selected compact non-Abelian Yang–Mills model. The model fixes the global form of $G$, its local bundle sector, the invariant quadratic form, matter representations, physical units, and boundary data. In the chosen local trivialization on oriented, time-oriented Minkowski space with signature $(-,+,+,+)$ and $x^0=ct$, use the curvature convention $F_A=dA+\tfrac12[A\wedge A]$ and the adopted Lorentzian action $S_0[A,\psi]=-\frac{1}{2g_{\rm YM}^2}\int\langle F_A\wedge *F_A\rangle+S_{\rm m}[A,\psi]$, where $g_{\rm YM}>0$ is dimensionless in four-dimensional natural units and $S_{\rm m}$ is the model-selected gauge-covariant matter action, or zero in the pure-gauge case. Set $c=\hbar=1$ in the perturbative formulas. The local field algebra contains the model-selected matter fields and the non-Abelian gauge potential $A_\mu$; the BRST convention is $sA_\mu=D_\mu c=\partial_\mu c+[A_\mu,c]$, $sc=-\tfrac12[c,c]$, and $s\psi=-\rho(c)\psi$. In the optional nonminimal sector $s\bar c=b$ and $sb=0$. Use Lorenz gauge $\partial^\mu A_\mu=0$ with $\xi>0$, dimensional regularization $D=4-2\epsilon$, modified minimal subtraction, and the stated finite engineering-dimension counterterm bound $d_*$. The classical gauge-invariance result for the selected action is a separate conditional supplier; the classical BV functional $\Gamma_0$ is an even ghost-number-zero input satisfying $\tfrac12(\Gamma_0,\Gamma_0)=0$. The chosen local BV functional domain has no nonzero central element of ghost number one.
