+## Definition
+
+Use a compact non-Abelian Lie group $G$, its Lie algebra $\mathfrak g$, a local gauge potential $A_\mu$ and the finite collection of matter fields and representations selected by the adopted Yang–Mills model. Work in a local trivialization of the selected bundle sector on oriented, time-oriented Minkowski space with signature $(-,+,+,+)$ and coordinates $x^0=ct$. With the alternating wedge–Lie bracket fixed by the principal-curvature supplier, write $F_A=dA+\tfrac12[A\wedge A]$. The adopted Lorentzian gauge action is $S_{\rm YM}[A]=-(2g_{\rm YM}^2)^{-1}\int\langle F_A\wedge *F_A\rangle$, with positive dimensionless $g_{\rm YM}$ and positive $\operatorname{Ad}$-invariant inner product; a model-supplied matter action is added when matter is present. For the formal perturbative formulas set $c=\hbar=1$; $A_\mu$ and $g_{\rm YM}$ have canonical engineering dimensions $1$ and $0$ in mass units. Give the ghost $c$ dimension $0$, the antighost $\bar c$ and auxiliary field $b$ dimension $2$, and the BRST differential dimension $0$. The matter-field dimensions are those assigned by the model's chosen kinetic terms; assign each antifield the dimension making its product with the corresponding BRST variation have density dimension $4$. The model supplies the physical units before this normalization and boundary conditions. The adopted model postulate and the classical gauge-invariance result supply the gauge action and its gauge-invariant interpretation; this definition does not prove either supplier.
+
+In the chosen local trivialization write $D_\mu c=\partial_\mu c+[A_\mu,c]$ and choose the linear covariant gauge condition $G(A)=\partial^\mu A_\mu=0$ with gauge parameter $\xi>0$. The nonminimal BRST variables are an odd antighost $\bar c$ of ghost number $-1$ and an even auxiliary field $b$ of ghost number $0$, with $s\bar c=b$ and $sb=0$. The gauge-fixing fermion and gauge-fixing contribution are
+
+$$\Psi_\xi=\int d^4x\,\langle\bar c,\partial^\mu A_\mu+\tfrac{\xi}{2}b\rangle,\qquad S_{\rm gf}:=s\Psi_\xi.$$
+
+Here $s$ is the odd BRST derivation on the finite-jet field algebra, extended to the nonminimal variables and their antifields using the specified BV convention. The gauge condition is a local perturbative choice; it does not assert a global slice or remove all gauge copies. A finite-dimensional regulated configuration space has an ordinary Faddeev–Popov Jacobian only when it supplies the finite-dimensional group action, gauge condition, and transverse slice data in the preceding finite-dimensional definition. Such a Jacobian is not a continuum functional determinant and does not define a continuum measure.
+
+A **formal perturbative renormalization datum** consists of the selected classical BV action $\Gamma_0$, the above gauge-fixing choice, the dimensional-regularization prescription $D=4-2\epsilon$, modified minimal subtraction of the $1/\epsilon$ poles together with $-\gamma_E+\log(4\pi)$, and a local counterterm space $\mathcal C_{\leq d_*}$. Here $d_*$ is a finite engineering-dimension bound fixed by the selected power-counting prescription; $\mathcal C_{\leq d_*}$ consists of integrated Lorentz-scalar polynomials of ghost number zero and engineering dimension at most $d_*$ in the fields, ghosts

